 "about": "Japanese cedar plantations and sweet pittosporum woods on the mid slopes, faya by the coasts, a few eucalyptus and maritime pines; remnant laurel forest of Azores laurel and Azores holly, with Azores juniper, Azores heather and Azores blueberry in the wet uplands up to the heath on Pico; hydrangea hedges along the roads and fields, kahili ginger and chain fern under the trees, bracken and agapanthus on the verges, heather on the upland heaths; black-and-white dairy cattle on the pastures and a few brown beef cattle; white houses with orange tile roofs and basalt trim. The vines in Pico's lava-walled currais have no model.",
